There is a difference between merely hitting stuff a lot, and having a
ridiculously high hit rate. There are also many low/mid monsters (i.e.
ants, bees, and xans) that are much easier to kill when you have a
maxed out luckstone.

A stack of poisoned darts is broken with a maxed out luckstone, since
the darts go from "disappears way too much to be useful" to
"disappears almost never".  Daggers wieght too much to carry a large
stack of them, but I can easily carry 100+ darts wherever I go.

Monks get automatic searching.  Combining that with a maxed out
luckstone means that you really almost never stumble into a trap.
This is meaningful since most Monks will not have magic resistance at
that time, and the risk of a polytrap destroying your armor drops down
to almost 0% with a maxed out luckstone.  Being able to easily detect
polytraps is also very useful because you'll have a higher chance of
being able to find-and-disable a polytrap before random monsters jump
into it.




